# Tooltip default (LOCKED)

When creating a tooltip, use the lock in
`src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/ExItS.PinoyBusinessPOS.React/src/features/ui-standards/tooltip-global-default.ts`.

The locked command is `ext tooltip soft-glass top`.

- Component: `ExitsTooltip` (portaled Soft Glass surface + triangle caret)
- Shell: Soft Glass (`TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_SHELL` = `soft-glass`) — theme primary wash via `data-shell="soft-glass"` on `.exits-tooltip`
- Placement: `top` (`TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_DEFAULT_PLACEMENT`) for table / toolbar / icon actions
- Sidebars (compact icon rail): pass `placement="end"` (or `start` in RTL layouts that need it)
- Delays: hover `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_HOVER_DELAY_MS` (300), focus `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_FOCUS_DELAY_MS` (40)
- Gap / caret: `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_GAP_PX` (10) / `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_ARROW_PX` (8) — keep `.exits-tooltip__arrow` CSS aligned
- Type: `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_FONT_SIZE` = **0.75rem**, `TOOLTIP_GLOBAL_FONT_WEIGHT` = **400** (not bold) — keep `.exits-tooltip` CSS aligned
- Accessibility: keep `aria-label` (or visible text) on the trigger; tooltip is supplementary only
- Do **not** rely on native `title=` alone for icon-only actions (browser tip competes with Soft Glass)

Use `ExitsTooltip` / `TableActionButton` (already wraps it). Do not invent a new tip surface, flat Material tip, or blur Soft Glass unless the user names one.

Change this lock only when the user asks. Update `tooltip-global-default.ts`, `tooltip-global-default.test.ts`, `ExitsTooltip.tsx`, and `.exits-tooltip` CSS in `globals.css` together.
